cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "QRAMP: cryptographic asset inventory and quantum-resistant migration planning"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Zhang"
    given-names: "Ti"
    email: "21111104@bjtu.edu.cn"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-6137-4350"
    affiliation: "Beijing Key Laboratory of Security and Privacy in Intelligent Transportation, Beijing Jiaotong University, Beijing 100044, China"
version: 0.1.1
date-released: 2026-10-20
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23487117"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Zhangtijerry/QRAMP"
abstract: "QRAMP collects cryptographic evidence from source code, SBOMs, X.509 certificates, configurations and TLS endpoints; resolves it into a CycloneDX cryptographic bill of materials (CBOM); classifies each asset with Mosca-inequality urgency; compiles a phased migration plan; and checks task acceptance against supplied scan evidence with explicit manual and deferred outcomes."
keywords:
  - post-quantum
  - cryptography
  - cbom
  - crypto-agility
  - security

